]}, "overview": "Wisconsin's 1st District is one of the most competitive House races of 2026. Republican incumbent Bryan Steil seeks another term in a seat with a slight Republican lean that has been in GOP hands for decades. Democrat Mitchell Berman has kept the race close, though Steil holds a large fundraising advantage with more than $2.2 million on hand.\n\nRecent polls from September and early October show the candidates essentially tied, though the data is sparse and partly sponsored by partisan groups. Expert ratings split between Lean R and Tossup, with one outlet calling it Lean D, and prediction markets price the race near even. The Democratic-tilted national environment offsets Steil's incumbency and financial edge, leaving the outcome genuinely uncertain heading into Election Day.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.3311, "margin": -2.62}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3005, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3258, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3559, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2698, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2844, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2996, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3365, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3287, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3978, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3557, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4029, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3963, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3263, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3374, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3619, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3249, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.3362, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.3278, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.3271, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.3986, 